In linux we can copy files from one locaation to another using command lines

we use the command "cp" to do this

Syntax:
cp file_name destination_Where_you_want_to_Copy_your_file

for eg if I have 2 directories, lbef and Personal and lbef contains a file name "Details" that I want in Personal as well then my command line
would be:

cp Details /home/kali/desktop/Personal

We can also copy multiple files at once, as follow

Syntax
cp file1 file2 file3 file4 /destination

We can also copy directory with cp

Syntax
cp -r d1 d2 d3 /destination

This is how we copy file from one loaction to another.
